                              "Ska du ta med det?"@sv ,
                              "Ist das zum Mitnehmen?"@de ,
                              "¿Es para llevar?"@es ,
                              "C'est à emporter ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 가져가실 거예요? or 포장해 드릴까요?; 드시고 means having it here."@en ,
                              "Det vore 가져가실 거예요? eller 포장해 드릴까요?; 드시고 betyder att man tar det här."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 가져가실 거예요? oder 포장해 드릴까요?; 드시고 heißt, es hier zu sich zu nehmen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 가져가실 거예요? o 포장해 드릴까요?; 드시고 significa tomarlo aquí."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 가져가실 거예요? ou 포장해 드릴까요? ; 드시고 veut dire le consommer sur place."@fr .

<#q-cafe-2c-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Did you enjoy it?"@en ,
                              "Smakade det bra?"@sv ,
                              "Hat es Ihnen geschmeckt?"@de ,
                              "¿Le ha gustado?"@es ,
                              "Ça vous a plu ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 맛있게 드셨어요?; 드시고 가세요? is asked before you eat or drink, not after."@en ,
                              "Det vore 맛있게 드셨어요?; 드시고 가세요? frågas innan man äter eller dricker, inte efteråt."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 맛있게 드셨어요?; 드시고 가세요? fragt man vor dem Essen oder Trinken, nicht danach."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 맛있게 드셨어요?; 드시고 가세요? se pregunta antes de comer o beber, no después."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 맛있게 드셨어요? ; 드시고 가세요? se demande avant de manger ou de boire, pas après."@fr .

<#ch-cafe-3>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-cafe> ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Same age?

*Another way it goes: drinks in hand, Alex and Minji sit down, and the talk soon turns to age.*

**민지:** 알렉스 씨, 실례지만 몇 년생이에요?\\
*Alex, if you don't mind me asking, what year were you born?*

**알렉스:** 98년생이에요. 민지 씨는요?\\
*1998. And you?*

**민지:** 어, 저도 98년생이에요. 우리 동갑이네요.\\
*Oh, me too. We're the same age.*

**알렉스:** 정말요? 신기하네요.\\
*Really? What a coincidence.*

---

**Why age comes up so early.** In Korean, age decides how people speak to each other: who uses which speech level, and who calls whom 언니, 오빠, 누나 or 형. So the question is not nosy; it tells both sides how to talk.

**몇 년생이에요?**: "What year were you born?" It is more exact than 몇 살이에요?, which you know from Everyday Korean phrases. To someone who may be older, say 몇 년생이세요?, with -시-. Since 2023, laws and official papers use international age, but many people still count the traditional way, so a birth year avoids confusion. You answer with two digits: 98년생 is read 구팔년생. 실례지만 (excuse me, but) makes a personal question gentler.

**우리 동갑이네요**: "We're the same age." 동갑 means born in the same year, and -네요 marks something you have just found out.

**Same age, same style?** Not yet. Being 동갑 makes friendship easier, and friends of the same age often switch to 반말, the casual style. But one of them has to suggest it first, so Alex and Minji stay with 해요체 for now."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-cafe-3a> ,
                         <#q-cafe-3b> .

<#q-cafe-3a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "몇 년생이에요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "What year were you born?"@en ,
                    "Vilket år är du född?"@sv ,
                    "In welchem Jahr bist du geboren?"@de ,
                    "¿En qué año naciste?"@es ,
                    "Tu es de quelle année ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Asked between new acquaintances of about the same generation, in polite 해요체, to find out who is older. It is more exact than 몇 살이에요?, since people count age in different ways. You answer with the last two digits: 98년생이에요, read 구팔년생이에요. To someone who may be older, say 몇 년생이세요?, with -시-."@en ,
                        "Frågas mellan nya bekanta i ungefär samma generation, i artig 해요체, för att ta reda på vem som är äldst. Det är exaktare än 몇 살이에요?, eftersom man räknar ålder på olika sätt. Man svarar med de två sista siffrorna: 98년생이에요, som läses 구팔년생이에요. Till någon som kan vara äldre säger man 몇 년생이세요?, med -시-."@sv ,
                        "Fragen sich neue Bekannte etwa derselben Generation, im höflichen 해요체, um herauszufinden, wer älter ist. Es ist genauer als 몇 살이에요?, weil das Alter unterschiedlich gezählt wird. Man antwortet mit den letzten zwei Ziffern: 98년생이에요, gelesen 구팔년생이에요. Zu jemandem, der älter sein könnte, sagt man 몇 년생이세요?, mit -시-."@de ,
                        "Lo preguntan nuevos conocidos de una generación parecida, en el estilo cortés 해요체, para saber quién es mayor. Es más exacto que 몇 살이에요?, porque la edad se cuenta de distintas maneras. Se responde con las dos últimas cifras: 98년생이에요, que se lee 구팔년생이에요. A alguien que puede ser mayor se le dice 몇 년생이세요?, con -시-."@es ,
                        "Se demande entre nouvelles connaissances d'à peu près la même génération, au style poli 해요체, pour savoir qui est l'aîné. C'est plus précis que 몇 살이에요?, car l'âge se compte de plusieurs façons. On répond avec les deux derniers chiffres : 98년생이에요, qui se lit 구팔년생이에요. À quelqu'un qui pourrait être plus âgé, on dit 몇 년생이세요?, avec -시-."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-cafe-3a-d1> ,
                          <#q-cafe-3a-d2> ,
                          <#q-cafe-3a-d3> .

<#q-cafe-3a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "When is your birthday?"@en ,
                              "När fyller du år?"@sv ,
                              "Wann hast du Geburtstag?"@de ,
                              "¿Cuándo es tu cumpleaños?"@es ,
                              "C'est quand, ton anniversaire ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 생일이 언제예요?; 년생 asks only for the year."@en ,
                              "Det vore 생일이 언제예요?; 년생 frågar bara efter året."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 생일이 언제예요?; 년생 fragt nur nach dem Jahr."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 생일이 언제예요?; 년생 pregunta solo por el año."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 생일이 언제예요? ; 년생 ne demande que l'année."@fr .

<#q-cafe-3a-d2>
