      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Please return the buzzer when you leave"@en ,
                              "Lämna tillbaka summern när du går"@sv ,
                              "Bitte geben Sie den Pager beim Gehen zurück"@de ,
                              "Devuelva el avisador al salir"@es ,
                              "Rendez le bipeur en partant"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 나가실 때 진동벨을 반납해 주세요; 울리면 means when it goes off."@en ,
                              "Det vore 나가실 때 진동벨을 반납해 주세요; 울리면 betyder när den surrar."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 나가실 때 진동벨을 반납해 주세요; 울리면 heißt, wenn er vibriert."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 나가실 때 진동벨을 반납해 주세요; 울리면 significa cuando suene."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 나가실 때 진동벨을 반납해 주세요 ; 울리면 veut dire quand il sonne."@fr .

<#q-cafe-r02-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Please come and pay when the buzzer goes off"@en ,
                              "Kom och betala när summern surrar"@sv ,
                              "Bitte kommen Sie zum Bezahlen, wenn der Pager vibriert"@de ,
                              "Venga a pagar cuando suene el avisador"@es ,
                              "Venez payer quand le bipeur sonne"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 진동벨이 울리면 계산하러 오세요; 가지러 means to fetch something."@en ,
                              "Det vore 진동벨이 울리면 계산하러 오세요; 가지러 betyder för att hämta något."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 진동벨이 울리면 계산하러 오세요; 가지러 heißt, um etwas abzuholen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 진동벨이 울리면 계산하러 오세요; 가지러 significa a recoger algo."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 진동벨이 울리면 계산하러 오세요 ; 가지러 veut dire pour venir chercher quelque chose."@fr .

# Chapter 1: What shall we eat?
<#ch-choose>
    a solid-memo:Chapter ,
      schema:Syllabus ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <> ;
    schema:position 1 ;
    dcterms:title "What shall we eat?"@en ,
                  "Vad ska vi äta?"@sv ,
                  "Was essen wir?"@de ,
                  "¿Qué comemos?"@es ,
                  "On mange quoi ?"@fr ,
                  "뭐 먹을까요?"@ko ;
    dcterms:description "Alex and Minji decide where to have dinner: suggesting and inviting, asking about spicy food and good places nearby, and saying what you don't or can't eat. Ends with a review of the chapter."@en ,
                        "Alex och Minji bestämmer var de ska äta middag: att föreslå och bjuda in, fråga om stark mat och bra ställen i närheten, och säga vad man inte äter eller inte kan äta. Avslutas med en repetition av kapitlet."@sv ,
                        "Alex und Minji entscheiden, wo sie zu Abend essen: vorschlagen und einladen, nach scharfem Essen und guten Lokalen in der Nähe fragen und sagen, was man nicht isst oder nicht essen kann. Endet mit einer Wiederholung des Kapitels."@de ,
                        "Alex y Minji deciden dónde cenar: proponer e invitar, preguntar por el picante y por buenos sitios cercanos, y decir lo que no comes o no puedes comer. Termina con un repaso del capítulo."@es ,
                        "Alex et Minji choisissent où dîner : proposer et inviter, demander si l'autre supporte le piquant et connaît un bon restaurant près d'ici, et dire ce que l'on ne mange pas ou ne peut pas manger. Se termine par une révision du chapitre."@fr ;
    solid-memo:reviewQuestion <#q-choose-r01> ,
                              <#q-choose-r02> .

<#ch-choose-1>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-choose> ;
    schema:position 0 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Choosing dinner

*Five o'clock, still at the café near Hongik University station. Alex and Minji have been talking for three hours.*

**민지:** 벌써 다섯 시네요! 저녁 뭐 먹을까요?\\
*Five o'clock already! What shall we have for dinner?*

**알렉스:** 좋아요. 그런데 저는 이 동네를 잘 몰라요. 이 근처에 맛집 알아요?\\
*Good idea. But I don't know this area well. Do you know a good place to eat around here?*

**민지:** 그럼요, 많이 알아요. 그런데 매운 거 잘 먹어요?\\
*Of course, lots. But can you handle spicy food?*

**알렉스:** 조금요. 너무 매운 건 힘들어요.\\
*A little. Really spicy food is hard for me.*

**민지:** 그럼 떡볶이는 다음에 먹어요. 뭐 못 먹는 거 있어요?\\
*Then let's save the spicy rice cakes for another day. Is there anything you can't eat?*

**알렉스:** 아니요, 없어요.\\
*No, nothing.*

**민지:** 그럼 찌개 먹으러 갈까요? 근처에 김치찌개 맛집이 있어요.\\
*Then shall we go and have stew? There's a great kimchi stew place nearby.*

**알렉스:** 좋아요, 가요!\\
*Great, let's go!*

---

**저녁 뭐 먹을까요?**: "What shall we have for dinner?" 저녁 is evening and also the evening meal; 뭐 is what. The ending -(으)ㄹ까요? asks the other person's opinion about something you would do together. The next step shows how it is built.

**이 근처에 맛집 알아요?**: "Do you know a good place to eat around here?" 맛집, literally "taste house", is a place known for its food. 이 근처에 means around here, as in 이 근처에 편의점 있어요?, which you know from Everyday Korean phrases.

**매운 거 잘 먹어요?**: "Can you handle spicy food?" Literally "do you eat spicy things well?": 잘 먹다 means to eat something happily and without trouble. Koreans ask it before choosing a place, together with 뭐 못 먹는 거 있어요? (is there anything you can't eat?). Alex and Minji still use 해요체."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-choose-1a> ,
                         <#q-choose-1b> ,
                         <#q-choose-1c> .

<#q-choose-1a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "저녁 뭐 먹을까요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "What shall we have for dinner?"@en ,
                    "Vad ska vi äta till middag?"@sv ,
                    "Was essen wir heute Abend?"@de ,
                    "¿Qué cenamos?"@es ,
                    "On mange quoi ce soir ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Said to a friend or acquaintance when suggesting dinner together, in polite 해요체. 저녁 is evening and also dinner; -(으)ㄹ까요? asks the other person's opinion about something you would do together. The answer is usually a suggestion, such as 찌개 어때요?"@en ,
                        "Sägs till en vän eller bekant när man föreslår att äta middag tillsammans, i artig 해요체. 저녁 är kväll och även middag; -(으)ㄹ까요? frågar vad den andra tycker om något ni skulle göra tillsammans. Svaret är oftast ett förslag, till exempel 찌개 어때요?"@sv ,
                        "Sagt man zu Freunden oder Bekannten, wenn man vorschlägt, zusammen zu Abend zu essen, im höflichen 해요체. 저녁 heißt Abend und auch Abendessen; -(으)ㄹ까요? fragt nach der Meinung des anderen zu etwas, das man gemeinsam tun würde. Die Antwort ist meist ein Vorschlag, etwa 찌개 어때요?"@de ,
                        "Se dice a un amigo o conocido al proponer cenar juntos, en el estilo cortés 해요체. 저녁 es la tarde-noche y también la cena; -(으)ㄹ까요? pide la opinión del otro sobre algo que haríais juntos. La respuesta suele ser una propuesta, como 찌개 어때요?"@es ,
                        "Dit à un ami ou une connaissance pour proposer de dîner ensemble, au style poli 해요체. 저녁 veut dire le soir et aussi le dîner ; -(으)ㄹ까요? demande l'avis de l'autre sur une chose à faire ensemble. La réponse est souvent une proposition, comme 찌개 어때요?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-choose-1a-d1> ,
                          <#q-choose-1a-d2> ,
                          <#q-choose-1a-d3> .

<#q-choose-1a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "What did you have for dinner?"@en ,
                              "Vad åt du till middag?"@sv ,
                              "Was hast du zu Abend gegessen?"@de ,
                              "¿Qué cenaste?"@es ,
                              "Tu as mangé quoi ce soir ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 저녁 뭐 먹었어요?: -었어요 is the past, while -(으)ㄹ까요? suggests something still to do."@en ,
                              "Det vore 저녁 뭐 먹었어요?: -었어요 är dåtid, medan -(으)ㄹ까요? föreslår något som ännu inte är gjort."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 저녁 뭐 먹었어요?: -었어요 ist die Vergangenheit, -(으)ㄹ까요? schlägt dagegen etwas vor, das noch kommt."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 저녁 뭐 먹었어요?: -었어요 es pasado, mientras que -(으)ㄹ까요? propone algo que aún está por hacer."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 저녁 뭐 먹었어요? : -었어요 est le passé, alors que -(으)ㄹ까요? propose une chose encore à faire."@fr .

<#q-choose-1a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Where shall we have dinner?"@en ,
                              "Var ska vi äta middag?"@sv ,
                              "Wo essen wir heute Abend?"@de ,
                              "¿Dónde cenamos?"@es ,
                              "On mange où ce soir ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 저녁 어디에서 먹을까요?: 뭐 asks what, 어디에서 asks where."@en ,
                              "Det vore 저녁 어디에서 먹을까요?: 뭐 frågar vad, 어디에서 frågar var."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 저녁 어디에서 먹을까요?: 뭐 fragt nach dem Was, 어디에서 nach dem Wo."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 저녁 어디에서 먹을까요?: 뭐 pregunta qué, 어디에서 pregunta dónde."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 저녁 어디에서 먹을까요? : 뭐 demande quoi, 어디에서 demande où."@fr .

<#q-choose-1a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "What shall we have for lunch?"@en ,
                              "Vad ska vi äta till lunch?"@sv ,
                              "Was essen wir zu Mittag?"@de ,
                              "¿Qué almorzamos?"@es ,
                              "On mange quoi ce midi ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 점심 뭐 먹을까요?: 점심 is lunch, 저녁 is dinner."@en ,
                              "Det vore 점심 뭐 먹을까요?: 점심 är lunch, 저녁 är middag."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 점심 뭐 먹을까요?: 점심 ist das Mittagessen, 저녁 das Abendessen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 점심 뭐 먹을까요?: 점심 es el almuerzo, 저녁 la cena."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 점심 뭐 먹을까요? : 점심 est le déjeuner, 저녁 le dîner."@fr .

<#q-choose-1b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "이 근처에 맛집 알아요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "Do you know a good place to eat around here?"@en ,
                    "Vet du något bra matställe här i närheten?"@sv ,
                    "Kennst du hier in der Nähe ein gutes Lokal?"@de ,
                    "¿Conoces algún buen sitio para comer por aquí?"@es ,
                    "Tu connais un bon restaurant dans le coin ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Asked when looking for somewhere to eat, in polite 해요체. 맛집, literally \"taste house\", is a place known for its good food; 이 근처에 means around here. The answer might be 네, 하나 알아요 or 글쎄요, 잘 모르겠어요."@en ,
                        "Frågas när man letar efter ett ställe att äta på, i artig 해요체. 맛집, ordagrant ”smakhus”, är ett ställe känt för sin goda mat; 이 근처에 betyder här i närheten. Svaret kan vara 네, 하나 알아요 eller 글쎄요, 잘 모르겠어요."@sv ,
                        "Fragt man, wenn man einen Ort zum Essen sucht, im höflichen 해요체. 맛집, wörtlich „Geschmackshaus“, ist ein Lokal, das für gutes Essen bekannt ist; 이 근처에 heißt hier in der Nähe. Die Antwort kann 네, 하나 알아요 oder 글쎄요, 잘 모르겠어요 sein."@de ,
                        "Se pregunta al buscar un sitio para comer, en el estilo cortés 해요체. 맛집, literalmente «casa del sabor», es un local conocido por su buena comida; 이 근처에 significa por aquí cerca. La respuesta puede ser 네, 하나 알아요 o 글쎄요, 잘 모르겠어요."@es ,
                        "Se demande quand on cherche où manger, au style poli 해요체. 맛집, littéralement « maison du goût », est une adresse connue pour sa bonne cuisine ; 이 근처에 veut dire près d'ici. La réponse peut être 네, 하나 알아요 ou 글쎄요, 잘 모르겠어요."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-choose-1b-d1> ,
                          <#q-choose-1b-d2> ,
                          <#q-choose-1b-d3> .

<#q-choose-1b-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Is there a convenience store around here?"@en ,
                              "Finns det en närbutik här i närheten?"@sv ,
                              "Gibt es hier in der Nähe einen kleinen Supermarkt?"@de ,
                              "¿Hay una tienda de conveniencia por aquí?"@es ,
                              "Il y a une supérette dans le coin ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 이 근처에 편의점 있어요?, which you know from Everyday Korean phrases; 맛집 is a good place to eat."@en ,
                              "Det vore 이 근처에 편의점 있어요?, som du känner från Koreanska vardagsfraser; 맛집 är ett bra matställe."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 이 근처에 편의점 있어요?, das du aus Koreanische Alltagswendungen kennst; 맛집 ist ein gutes Lokal."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 이 근처에 편의점 있어요?, que conoces de Frases coreanas cotidianas; 맛집 es un buen sitio para comer."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 이 근처에 편의점 있어요?, que tu connais grâce à Expressions coréennes du quotidien ; 맛집 est une bonne adresse pour manger."@fr .

<#q-choose-1b-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Do you live around here?"@en ,
                              "Bor du här i närheten?"@sv ,
                              "Wohnst du hier in der Nähe?"@de ,
                              "¿Vives por aquí?"@es ,
                              "Tu habites dans le coin ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 이 근처에 살아요?: 알다 is to know, 살다 is to live."@en ,
                              "Det vore 이 근처에 살아요?: 알다 är att veta eller känna till, 살다 är att bo."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 이 근처에 살아요?: 알다 heißt kennen oder wissen, 살다 wohnen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 이 근처에 살아요?: 알다 es conocer o saber, 살다 es vivir."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 이 근처에 살아요? : 알다 veut dire connaître ou savoir, 살다 habiter."@fr .

<#q-choose-1b-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Do you know the way to the restaurant?"@en ,
                              "Hittar du till restaurangen?"@sv ,
                              "Kennst du den Weg zum Restaurant?"@de ,
                              "¿Sabes cómo llegar al restaurante?"@es ,
                              "Tu sais comment aller au restaurant ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 식당에 가는 길 알아요?; 맛집 알아요? asks for a recommendation, not for directions."@en ,
                              "Det vore 식당에 가는 길 알아요?; 맛집 알아요? ber om ett tips, inte om vägen."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 식당에 가는 길 알아요?; 맛집 알아요? fragt nach einer Empfehlung, nicht nach dem Weg."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 식당에 가는 길 알아요?; 맛집 알아요? pide una recomendación, no el camino."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 식당에 가는 길 알아요? ; 맛집 알아요? demande une recommandation, pas le chemin."@fr .

<#q-choose-1c>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "매운 거 잘 먹어요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "Can you handle spicy food?"@en ,
                    "Klarar du stark mat?"@sv ,
                    "Verträgst du scharfes Essen?"@de ,
                    "¿Llevas bien el picante?"@es ,
                    "Tu supportes bien le piquant ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "Asked by a Korean friend or host before choosing where or what to eat, in polite 해요체. Literally \"do you eat spicy things well?\": 잘 먹다 means to eat something happily. Answer 네, 잘 먹어요 or 매운 건 잘 못 먹어요."@en ,
                        "Frågas av en koreansk vän eller värd innan man väljer var eller vad man ska äta, i artig 해요체. Ordagrant ”äter du starka saker bra?”: 잘 먹다 betyder att äta något med god aptit. Svara 네, 잘 먹어요 eller 매운 건 잘 못 먹어요."@sv ,
                        "Fragt ein koreanischer Freund oder Gastgeber, bevor man wählt, wo oder was man isst, im höflichen 해요체. Wörtlich „isst du scharfe Sachen gut?“: 잘 먹다 heißt, etwas gern und mit Appetit essen. Antwort: 네, 잘 먹어요 oder 매운 건 잘 못 먹어요."@de ,
                        "Lo pregunta un amigo o anfitrión coreano antes de elegir dónde o qué comer, en el estilo cortés 해요체. Literalmente «¿comes bien cosas picantes?»: 잘 먹다 es comer algo con gusto. Se responde 네, 잘 먹어요 o 매운 건 잘 못 먹어요."@es ,
                        "Demandé par un ami ou un hôte coréen avant de choisir où ou quoi manger, au style poli 해요체. Littéralement « tu manges bien les choses piquantes ? » : 잘 먹다 veut dire manger quelque chose avec plaisir. On répond 네, 잘 먹어요 ou 매운 건 잘 못 먹어요."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-choose-1c-d1> ,
                          <#q-choose-1c-d2> ,
                          <#q-choose-1c-d3> .

<#q-choose-1c-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Is this dish very spicy?"@en ,
                              "Är den här rätten väldigt stark?"@sv ,
                              "Ist dieses Gericht sehr scharf?"@de ,
                              "¿Este plato pica mucho?"@es ,
                              "Ce plat est très piquant ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 이 음식 많이 매워요? (매워요? you know from Everyday Korean phrases); 매운 거 잘 먹어요? asks about the person, not the dish."@en ,
                              "Det vore 이 음식 많이 매워요? (매워요? känner du från Koreanska vardagsfraser); 매운 거 잘 먹어요? frågar om personen, inte om rätten."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 이 음식 많이 매워요? (매워요? kennst du aus Koreanische Alltagswendungen); 매운 거 잘 먹어요? fragt nach der Person, nicht nach dem Gericht."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 이 음식 많이 매워요? (매워요? lo conoces de Frases coreanas cotidianas); 매운 거 잘 먹어요? pregunta por la persona, no por el plato."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 이 음식 많이 매워요? (tu connais 매워요? grâce à Expressions coréennes du quotidien) ; 매운 거 잘 먹어요? porte sur la personne, pas sur le plat."@fr .

<#q-choose-1c-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Do you eat a lot?"@en ,
                              "Äter du mycket?"@sv ,
                              "Isst du viel?"@de ,
                              "¿Comes mucho?"@es ,
                              "Tu manges beaucoup ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 많이 먹어요?; 잘 here means happily and without trouble, not a lot."@en ,
                              "Det vore 많이 먹어요?; 잘 betyder här gärna och utan problem, inte mycket."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 많이 먹어요?; 잘 heißt hier gern und ohne Probleme, nicht viel."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 많이 먹어요?; aquí 잘 significa con gusto y sin problema, no mucho."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 많이 먹어요? ; ici 잘 veut dire volontiers et sans problème, pas beaucoup."@fr .

<#q-choose-1c-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Do you like sweet things?"@en ,
                              "Gillar du sött?"@sv ,
                              "Magst du Süßes?"@de ,
                              "¿Te gusta lo dulce?"@es ,
                              "Tu aimes le sucré ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 단 거 좋아해요?: 맵다 is spicy, 달다 is sweet."@en ,
                              "Det vore 단 거 좋아해요?: 맵다 är stark, 달다 är söt."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 단 거 좋아해요?: 맵다 heißt scharf, 달다 süß."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 단 거 좋아해요?: 맵다 es picante, 달다 es dulce."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 단 거 좋아해요? : 맵다 veut dire piquant, 달다 sucré."@fr .

<#ch-choose-2>
    a solid-memo:Step ,
      schema:LearningResource ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    schema:isPartOf <#ch-choose> ;
    schema:position 1 ;
    solid-memo:textFormat solid-memo:markdown ;
    solid-memo:theory """## Shall we, or would you like to?

**-(으)ㄹ까요?** puts an idea up for the other person to decide: "shall we?" or "shall I?". Add -ㄹ까요 to a stem that ends in a vowel or ㄹ, and -을까요 after any other consonant: 가다 becomes 갈까요?, 만들다 becomes 만들까요?, 먹다 becomes 먹을까요?

**-(으)ㄹ래요?** asks what the other person wants: "do you want to?", "would you like to?". It is a warm invitation between peers. It is built the same way: 갈래요?, 만들래요?, 먹을래요? In an answer it says what you want: 저는 국수 먹을래요 (I'd like noodles).

**-(으)러 가다** means going somewhere to do something. Add -러 after a vowel or ㄹ and -으러 after another consonant: 먹으러 가요 (go to eat), 커피 마시러 가요 (go for a coffee).

**민지:** 비빔밥 먹으러 갈래요?\\
*Do you want to go and have bibimbap?*

**알렉스:** 좋아요. 지금 갈까요?\\
*Sure. Shall we go now?*

---

**안 and 못.** Both make a verb negative and stand right before it. 안 says you don't, by choice or habit. 못 says you can't: something stops you.

- **저는 고기를 안 먹어요**: "I don't eat meat." This is what a vegetarian says: a choice.
- **매운 건 잘 못 먹어요**: "I'm not good with spicy food." Literally "I can't eat spicy things well". This is the honest answer to 매운 거 잘 먹어요?

Say 고기를 못 먹어요 and you can't eat meat, perhaps for your health; say 매운 건 안 먹어요 and you choose not to.

**매운 건** is short for 매운 것은: 은 sets spicy food apart from the rest, as in "spicy food, I'm not good with". In the question it is 매운 거, short for 매운 것.

**잘 못** with a space means "not well". Written together, 잘못 means a mistake or wrongly: 잘못 먹었어요 is "I ate something that disagreed with me"."""@en ;
    solid-memo:checkedBy <#q-choose-2a> ,
                         <#q-choose-2b> ,
                         <#q-choose-2c> .

<#q-choose-2a>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "비빔밥 먹으러 갈래요?"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "Do you want to go and have bibimbap?"@en ,
                    "Vill du gå och äta bibimbap?"@sv ,
                    "Hast du Lust, Bibimbap essen zu gehen?"@de ,
                    "¿Quieres ir a comer bibimbap?"@es ,
                    "Tu veux aller manger un bibimbap ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "An invitation to a friend or acquaintance, in polite 해요체. -(으)러 가다 means going somewhere to do something, and -(으)ㄹ래요? asks what the other person would like. Answer 좋아요, 같이 가요! or, to say no gently, 오늘은 좀 그래요."@en ,
                        "En inbjudan till en vän eller bekant, i artig 해요체. -(으)러 가다 betyder att gå någonstans för att göra något, och -(으)ㄹ래요? frågar vad den andra vill. Svara 좋아요, 같이 가요! eller, för att säga nej vänligt, 오늘은 좀 그래요."@sv ,
                        "Eine Einladung an Freunde oder Bekannte, im höflichen 해요체. -(으)러 가다 heißt, irgendwohin gehen, um etwas zu tun, und -(으)ㄹ래요? fragt, was der andere möchte. Antwort: 좋아요, 같이 가요! oder, als sanftes Nein, 오늘은 좀 그래요."@de ,
                        "Una invitación a un amigo o conocido, en el estilo cortés 해요체. -(으)러 가다 es ir a algún sitio a hacer algo, y -(으)ㄹ래요? pregunta qué quiere el otro. Se responde 좋아요, 같이 가요! o, para decir que no con suavidad, 오늘은 좀 그래요."@es ,
                        "Une invitation à un ami ou une connaissance, au style poli 해요체. -(으)러 가다 veut dire aller quelque part pour faire quelque chose, et -(으)ㄹ래요? demande ce que l'autre veut. On répond 좋아요, 같이 가요! ou, pour refuser gentiment, 오늘은 좀 그래요."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-choose-2a-d1> ,
                          <#q-choose-2a-d2> ,
                          <#q-choose-2a-d3> .

<#q-choose-2a-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Have you ever had bibimbap?"@en ,
                              "Har du ätit bibimbap förut?"@sv ,
                              "Hast du schon mal Bibimbap gegessen?"@de ,
                              "¿Has comido bibimbap alguna vez?"@es ,
                              "Tu as déjà mangé un bibimbap ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 비빔밥 먹어 봤어요?; -(으)ㄹ래요? invites, it does not ask about the past."@en ,
                              "Det vore 비빔밥 먹어 봤어요?; -(으)ㄹ래요? bjuder in, den frågar inte om det som har hänt."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 비빔밥 먹어 봤어요?; -(으)ㄹ래요? lädt ein und fragt nicht nach der Vergangenheit."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 비빔밥 먹어 봤어요?; -(으)ㄹ래요? invita, no pregunta por el pasado."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 비빔밥 먹어 봤어요? ; -(으)ㄹ래요? invite, il ne porte pas sur le passé."@fr .

<#q-choose-2a-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Do you want to make bibimbap?"@en ,
                              "Vill du laga bibimbap?"@sv ,
                              "Willst du Bibimbap kochen?"@de ,
                              "¿Quieres preparar bibimbap?"@es ,
                              "Tu veux préparer un bibimbap ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 비빔밥 만들래요?; 먹으러 가다 is going out to eat, not cooking."@en ,
                              "Det vore 비빔밥 만들래요?; 먹으러 가다 är att gå ut och äta, inte att laga mat."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 비빔밥 만들래요?; 먹으러 가다 heißt essen gehen, nicht kochen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 비빔밥 만들래요?; 먹으러 가다 es salir a comer, no cocinar."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 비빔밥 만들래요? ; 먹으러 가다 veut dire aller manger dehors, pas cuisiner."@fr .

<#q-choose-2a-d3>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "Do you want bibimbap to take away?"@en ,
                              "Vill du ta med dig bibimbap?"@sv ,
                              "Willst du Bibimbap zum Mitnehmen?"@de ,
                              "¿Quieres bibimbap para llevar?"@es ,
                              "Tu veux un bibimbap à emporter ?"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 비빔밥 포장할래요?; nothing in 먹으러 가다 says take away."@en ,
                              "Det vore 비빔밥 포장할래요?; inget i 먹으러 가다 säger att ta med."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 비빔밥 포장할래요?; in 먹으러 가다 steckt nichts von Mitnehmen."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 비빔밥 포장할래요?; nada en 먹으러 가다 habla de llevar."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 비빔밥 포장할래요? ; rien dans 먹으러 가다 ne parle d'emporter."@fr .

<#q-choose-2b>
    a solid-memo:Card ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 5 ;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-16T12:00:00.000Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    solid-memo:front "매운 건 잘 못 먹어요"@ko ;
    solid-memo:back "I'm not good with spicy food"@en ,
                    "Jag tål inte stark mat så bra"@sv ,
                    "Scharfes vertrage ich nicht so gut"@de ,
                    "No llevo muy bien el picante"@es ,
                    "Je ne supporte pas très bien le piquant"@fr ;
    solid-memo:backNote "The usual answer to 매운 거 잘 먹어요? when spice is a problem, in polite 해요체. 못 says you can't rather than won't, and 잘 못 means not well; 매운 건 is short for 매운 것은. If you can handle it: 네, 잘 먹어요."@en ,
                        "Det vanliga svaret på 매운 거 잘 먹어요? när stark mat är ett problem, i artig 해요체. 못 säger att man inte kan, inte att man inte vill, och 잘 못 betyder inte så bra; 매운 건 är kort för 매운 것은. Klarar man det: 네, 잘 먹어요."@sv ,
                        "Die übliche Antwort auf 매운 거 잘 먹어요?, wenn Schärfe ein Problem ist, im höflichen 해요체. 못 sagt, dass man nicht kann, nicht dass man nicht will, und 잘 못 heißt nicht gut; 매운 건 ist kurz für 매운 것은. Wenn man es verträgt: 네, 잘 먹어요."@de ,
                        "La respuesta habitual a 매운 거 잘 먹어요? cuando el picante es un problema, en el estilo cortés 해요체. 못 dice que no puedes, no que no quieres, y 잘 못 significa no muy bien; 매운 건 es la forma corta de 매운 것은. Si lo llevas bien: 네, 잘 먹어요."@es ,
                        "La réponse habituelle à 매운 거 잘 먹어요? quand le piquant pose problème, au style poli 해요체. 못 dit qu'on ne peut pas, pas qu'on ne veut pas, et 잘 못 veut dire pas bien ; 매운 건 est la forme courte de 매운 것은. Si on le supporte : 네, 잘 먹어요."@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractor <#q-choose-2b-d1> ,
                          <#q-choose-2b-d2> ,
                          <#q-choose-2b-d3> .

<#q-choose-2b-d1>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "I don't eat spicy food, on principle"@en ,
                              "Jag äter inte stark mat, av princip"@sv ,
                              "Scharfes esse ich aus Prinzip nicht"@de ,
                              "No como picante, por principio"@es ,
                              "Je ne mange pas de piquant, par principe"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 매운 건 안 먹어요: 안 is a choice, while 못 says you can't manage it."@en ,
                              "Det vore 매운 건 안 먹어요: 안 är ett val, medan 못 säger att man inte klarar det."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 매운 건 안 먹어요: 안 ist eine Entscheidung, 못 sagt dagegen, dass man es nicht schafft."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 매운 건 안 먹어요: 안 es una elección, mientras que 못 dice que no puedes con ello."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 매운 건 안 먹어요 : 안 est un choix, alors que 못 dit qu'on n'y arrive pas."@fr .

<#q-choose-2b-d2>
    a solid-memo:Distractor ,
      schema:Answer ;
    solid-memo:formatVersion 1 ;
    solid-memo:distractorText "It isn't very spicy"@en ,
                              "Det är inte särskilt starkt"@sv ,
                              "Das ist nicht besonders scharf"@de ,
                              "No pica mucho"@es ,
                              "Ce n'est pas très piquant"@fr ;
    solid-memo:distractorNote "That would be 별로 안 매워요; 매운 건 잘 못 먹어요 is about the speaker, not the dish."@en ,
                              "Det vore 별로 안 매워요; 매운 건 잘 못 먹어요 handlar om den som talar, inte om rätten."@sv ,
                              "Das wäre 별로 안 매워요; 매운 건 잘 못 먹어요 geht um die Person, nicht um das Gericht."@de ,
                              "Eso sería 별로 안 매워요; 매운 건 잘 못 먹어요 habla de quien lo dice, no del plato."@es ,
                              "Ce serait 별로 안 매워요 ; 매운 건 잘 못 먹어요 parle de la personne, pas du plat."@fr .

